# Day and night turn Brutal Cathar over (CR 702.145, 731), and transforming is not leaving the battlefield: Bot1 casts the
# Cathar on turn 3 and exiles Bot2's Ornithopter - a choice, since Bot2's Dryad Arbor, a land creature, is a target too.
# Bot2 casts nothing on turn 4, so it is night on turn 5 and the Cathar is Moonrage Brute, a 3/3 with first strike and
# ward-pay 3 life, with the Ornithopter still exiled. On turn 6 Bot2 targets the Brute with Giant Growth and pays 3 life
# (17), then with Lightning Bolt and does not pay, so the Bolt is countered. Bot2 has cast two spells on its turn, so on
# turn 7 it is day again, the Brute is the Cathar once more and "transforms into Brutal Cathar" exiles the Dryad Arbor, the
# lone target. Bot1 bolts its own Cathar, and both cards return together (CR 610.3).

